      "writtenOn": "2024-10-15T04:56:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Technically the wrong behavior for `code`, `entryPoint`, and `key` (nulls in strings should cause errors, rather than cut off at the null) but I think it\u0027s OK.\n\n(It\u0027s allowed for labels because they\u0027re sort of \"best effort\".)",
      "revId": "eff78ba86ddb1a8234d9be7cef14d851ebb9b98c",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "014920d3_c2010537",
        "filename": "third_party/emdawnwebgpu/library_webgpu.js",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 187,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000015
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-15T04:56:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this should only happen if `length` is also `WGPU_STRLEN`, otherwise it could be an empty string (`{nullptr, 0}`).\n\nUnfortunately `WGPU_STRLEN` has a variable value because of Memory64, and I do not know what value you will get if you read a `SIZE_MAX` as a `*` type... probably a BigInt `0xFFFF_FFFF_FFFF_FFFFn`?",
      "revId": "eff78ba86ddb1a8234d9be7cef14d851ebb9b98c",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cf510e85_06c5058c",
        "filename": "third_party/emdawnwebgpu/library_webgpu.js",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 187,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-15T07:55:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe for Emscripten we could have logic like:\n\n```\nif (!ptr) {\n    if (length \u003d\u003d 0) {\n        return \"\";\n    } else {\n        return undefined;\n    }\n}\nreturn UTF8ToString(ptr, length);\n```",
      "parentUuid": "014920d3_c2010537",
      "revId": "eff78ba86ddb1a8234d9be7cef14d851ebb9b98c",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3bfee3f1_14590e78",
        "filename": "third_party/emdawnwebgpu/library_webgpu.js",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 187,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000015
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-15T18:24:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m sure UTF8ToString can handle empty strings, but true we don\u0027t need to worry about the exact value of WGPU_STRLEN. I think we can just do `if (length \u0026\u0026 !ptr) { return undefined; }`\n\nthough it would be nice to crash if it\u0027s nullptr + an invalid length. I think `assert(ptr \u003e 0 || length \u003d\u003d 0 || length \u003e\u003d 0xffff_ffff)` since that should work for both values of WGPU_STRLEN",
      "parentUuid": "cf510e85_06c5058c",
      "revId": "eff78ba86ddb1a8234d9be7cef14d851ebb9b98c",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
