      "writtenOn": "2024-10-15T20:44:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I actually started with doing it unconditionally, but it didn\u0027t work? I think it might be the way that Blink handles the descriptor.. but not something that I could fix in this change. (I can investigate a bit more into that side afterwards.)\n\nTbf, it also doesn\u0027t make sense for `\"\"` to be an `entryPoint` anyways right? We only default if it\u0027s strictly `undefined` right now, i.e. it doesn\u0027t even work if we set `entryPoint \u003d undefined`, as per what I said above. Is it possible for `\"\"` to be a valid entry point?",
      "parentUuid": "7a5a1fd0_ee34a752",
